Drop two unused imports so GraMi builds on Java >= 11.

javax.jws (module java.xml.ws) and javax.rmi.CORBA (module java.corba) were removed
from the JDK in Java 11 (JEP 320, https://openjdk.org/jeps/320). Neither import is
used: the code calls utilities.Util.clone fully qualified. Applied to GraMi d2875ae8
inside the Docker image build only (docs/context/tooling/grami.md §3); the submodule
itself is never edited. Apply with: patch -p1 -d <grami> < this-file

--- a/GRAMI_DIRECTED_SUBGRAPHS/src/search/RightMostExtension.java
+++ b/GRAMI_DIRECTED_SUBGRAPHS/src/search/RightMostExtension.java
@@ -27,8 +27,6 @@
 import java.util.Map;
 import java.util.TreeMap;

-import javax.jws.Oneway;
-import javax.rmi.CORBA.Util;

 import utilities.MyPair;

--- a/GRAMI_UNDIRECTED_SUBGRAPHS/src/search/RightMostExtension.java
+++ b/GRAMI_UNDIRECTED_SUBGRAPHS/src/search/RightMostExtension.java
@@ -27,8 +27,6 @@
 import java.util.Map;
 import java.util.TreeMap;

-import javax.jws.Oneway;
-import javax.rmi.CORBA.Util;

 import utilities.MyPair;

